Artifact review caught a real audit-quality issue: redundancy removal could record a feature as “retained” and later remove that same representative through a correlation chain. The final selected set was still nonredundant enough for this run, but the explanation was not reliably truthful. I’m replacing that logic with score-ordered greedy representatives and adding a regression assertion before re-running everything and regenerating evidence.
